note How paths are placed in groups so the paths list is a tree instead of one flat list. A group is a field of the path, normalised by normal_group, with / nesting one group in another; a group exists while a path is in it. Map::rows orders the list once for both front ends: at each level the groups sorted by name, then the paths of that level in map order.

